# Blender 3.6 GPU Launcher for ChromeOS (Crostini)

A simple shell script to launch Blender 3.6+ on Chromebooks running Linux (Crostini) using hardware GPU acceleration (`virpipe`) instead of software rendering.

## Fixes
- Bypasses `EGL_BAD_MATCH` / `EGL_NOT_INITIALIZED` errors.
- Fixes `epoxy_get_proc_address` assertions.
- Routes rendering through X11 and Mesa Virpipe GPU driver.

## Usage
```bash
chmod +x launch-blender.sh
./launch-blender.sh
